{
  "id": "companion-publish",
  "title": "Compiled services publish to the page",
  "summary": "Native services, WebAssembly services and TypeScript or Dart browser services inject an `ApplicationEventPublisher` for local events. `OnEvent` receives the events, and `OnStart`/`OnStop` run when the service starts and stops. Call the publisher to publish an event. A listener that is not `InBackground` can also return a model value. The runtime then publishes it as the model named by the return type of the listener. Each activation gets a new ID. The runtime rejects callbacks from an old activation. Each example publishes a `CatalogCount` model when it starts and updates its count in a listener for that model. Ruby names the model of a listener in a YARD tag, # @param value [CatalogCount]. Lua names it in a LuaCATS tag, ---@param value CatalogCount, and publishes a model table, setmetatable({ count = 5 }, CatalogCount), through its application_event_publisher field. F# takes the publisher as a constructor parameter, `type CatalogService(applicationEventPublisher: ApplicationEventPublisher)`. The JavaScript `CatalogService` only listens, to events published by its native or WebAssembly counterpart.",
  "group": "Native",
